---
description: Keep Lunmi H5 and the LunmiBrafer iOS project synchronized
alwaysApply: true
---

After changing `lunmi_h5/src/**`, `static/**`, environment/configuration or build scripts:

1. Run `pnpm sync:ios` in `lunmi_h5`.
2. Run `pnpm check:ios-sync` and resolve any mismatch.
3. Run relevant tests. For native changes, also build the `LunmiBrafer` simulator scheme.

Do not edit generated `LunmiBrafer/LunmiBrafer/lunimcenter.bundledata` directly. This single file contains the encrypted manifest and double-compressed, AES-256-GCM encrypted resources; `--check` verifies its decrypted content as well as the source fingerprint. Do not restore a separate `manifest.json`, `lunimcenter/` resource directory or plaintext `Web/` resources. Keep the native package key paired with the package and do not print it.
H5 builds synchronize automatically. Use `pnpm watch:ios` for continuous editing.
Xcode directly copies `lunimcenter.bundledata` and reads the checked-in `LunmiBrafer/Info.plist`. The iOS project must build and archive without a `scripts/` directory, Node.js or H5 source. Do not add external-script build phases.
`pnpm sync:ios` also updates the narrow HTTP exception in Info.plist from the Swift API configuration; `pnpm check:ios-sync` verifies both resources and that configuration. Run both before Xcode builds or handoff.
Do not claim synchronization succeeded unless the content and source fingerprints match.
